\fs20 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw2
These scans were further altered and abstracted, marked by rippling, wave-like distortions that further fragment the visual plane. Building on the deconstruction of Ruth Bader Ginsburg\'92s image, this progression strips away familiar iconography to \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 challenge the viewer\'92s perception of identity and mythology. By employing \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw2
riso printing, scanning, and digital distortion, the series defamiliarizes static representations, inviting a reimagining and redefinition of the Crone as a fluid, multifaceted figure that defies societal constraints and expectations.\

\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \
The imagery of the Crone was created by abstracting the aging female form using riso, scanners, and digital methods. By defamiliarizing the viewer with the typical forms associated with old age, we can reimagine the crone's identity as more complex and fluid, transcending society's expectations.
